    reg {
        name = "L2 special check 0";
        desc = "ECC/check status 0; the interrupt handler prints it and the init code clears it (writes 0).

Vendor driver `arch/arm/mm/cache-hil2v200.c` / `cache-hil2v200.h` (REG_L2_SPECIAL_CHECK0). Read on hardware as 0x6DF7B1BE in the first read and as 0x6DF7B1BC on 2026-11-08 (stock U-Boot prompt after a cold boot): bit 1 differs between the two reads, so it is not a fixed constant. The reset stays 0x6DF7B1BE.";

        field {
            name = "value";
            desc = "Register value (layout not documented).";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x6DF7B1BE;
